tribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{80.44}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101520" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{85.33}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101520" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{80.44}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2,-1,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1,5,-2 \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/example-4327.json" "file_sha256" "d54021ef644f7b5a247e30e2c3fc9eb3555b9bc1c406195f79d008067ba64e20" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=-4$, find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle t, \\, -2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 6, \\, t \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/example-5112.json" "file_sha256" "356ecf4df1339dc2a4c44a754ee592b1e87a838e992cfecdca401222768cfd31" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(0,4,5)$, $Q(1,5,4)$, and $R(2,3,6).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae685cf4e881b26563a6ae4d8b2da04154e4434506f1e9823304e0edb7c0e824" "basis" 843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨0,4,5⟩,\\,q=⟨1,5,4⟩,\\,r=⟨2,3,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨1,5,4⟩-⟨0,4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨2,3,6⟩-⟨0,4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(0)={90}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae685cf4e881b26563a6ae4d8b2da04154e4434506f1e9823304e0edb7c0e824" "basis" 843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60cd1315cf2b6b75f4b50b0389fd8558a2160d0ff8f42305f4c35d7522a171fd" "basis" 843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae685cf4e881b26563a6ae4d8b2da04154e4434506f1e9823304e0edb7c0e824" "basis" 843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(2,-1,2)$, $B(3,-5,1)$, and $C(1,-4,-1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae685cf4e881b26563a6ae4d8b2da04154e4434506f1e9823304e0edb7c0e824" "basis" 843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,-1,2⟩,\\,b=⟨3,-5,1⟩,\\,c=⟨1,-4,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-5,1⟩-⟨2,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-4,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨1,-4,-1⟩-⟨2,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot (-3)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{18}\\cdot \\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3\\sqrt{38}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{14}{3\\sqrt{38}})≈{41}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae685cf4e881b26563a6ae4d8b2da04154e4434506f1e9823304e0edb7c0e824" "basis" 843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma